# Row actions menu

When a table or list row has **2 or more** action options (links or buttons), use `RowActionsMenu` — do not render a flat row of links.

Component: `@/app/components/_ui/resource/RowActionsMenu`  
Styles: `.row-menu*` in `src/app/globals.css`

## Rules

- **2+ visible actions** → `RowActionsMenu` with `items`
- **1 action** → plain `row-links` / `Link` / `text-link` is fine (`RowActionsMenu` also falls back to that)
- Prefer `href` for navigation; use `onClick` for side effects (health check, delete, etc.)
- Hide conditional items with `hidden: true` (do not leave empty slots)
- Keep trigger label default `"Ações"` unless the context needs another short label
- Do not reinvent dropdowns with rsuite `Whisper`/`Dropdown` or ad-hoc absolute menus for this pattern

## Example

```tsx
import { RowActionsMenu } from "@/app/components/_ui/resource/RowActionsMenu";

// ❌ BAD — flat links when there are 2+
<div className="row-links">
  <button type="button" className="text-link" onClick={onHealth}>Health</button>
  <Link href={`/provider/hotspots/${row.isp.id}`}>Do provedor</Link>
  <Link href={`/provider/hotspot/cadastro/${row.id}`}>Cadastro</Link>
  <Link href={`/provider/hotspot/show/${row.id}`}>Abrir</Link>
</div>

// ✅ GOOD
<RowActionsMenu
  items={[
    {
      key: "health",
      label: checking ? "Checando..." : "Health",
      onClick: () => onHealth(row.id),
      disabled: checking,
    },
    {
      key: "provider",
      label: "Do provedor",
      href: `/provider/hotspots/${row.isp?.id}`,
      hidden: !row.isp?.id,
    },
    { key: "cadastro", label: "Cadastro", href: `/provider/hotspot/cadastro/${row.id}` },
    { key: "abrir", label: "Abrir", href: `/provider/hotspot/show/${row.id}` },
  ]}
/>
```
